# Browser harness: dependencies and the scratch copy of the pinned specs are artifacts.
node_modules/
.pinned-run/
test-results/
generation-probe-report.json
# Per-run legs of the two-leg generation comparison, 100-250 KB each. They are evidence for
# one run, not an expectation: the committed artifact is generation-comparison.json, which
# records the DIFFERENCE. Committing a leg would invite someone to treat a known divergence
# as the expected value.
gen-a.json
gen-p1.json
# Per-run legs and captures of the two-leg comparisons (startup, streaming, cancel,
# non-stream). They are 100-250 KB each and are evidence for ONE run, not an expectation: the
# committed artifacts are *-comparison.json, which record the DIFFERENCES and the checks. A
# committed leg invites someone to treat a known divergence as the expected value.
startup-gotavern-*.json
startup-pinned-*.json
stream-gotavern.json
stream-pinned.json
cancel-gotavern.json
cancel-pinned.json
nonstream-gotavern.json
nonstream-pinned.json
# Per-run legs of the extension E2E (Tavern Helper / JS-Slash-Runner). Same reasoning as the legs above:
# the committed artifact is extension-tavern-helper-comparison.json, which records the DIFFERENCES and
# the guards. A committed leg here would be 60-210 KB of one run's evidence and invite treating a known
# divergence as the expected value.
extension-tavern-helper-gotavern.json
extension-tavern-helper-pinned.json
extension-littlewhitebox-gotavern.json
extension-littlewhitebox-pinned.json
# Per-run legs of the data-domain drive (characters, chats, settings, backgrounds, quick replies).
# Same reasoning: the committed artifact is data-domain-comparison.json, which records the interactions,
# the write evidence and the guards. A committed leg is one run's evidence, not an expectation.
data-domain-gotavern-*.json
data-domain-pinned-*.json